<title>USA: U.S. soy export numbers slightly disappointing.</title>
<headline>U.S. soy export numbers slightly disappointing.</headline>
<byline>Bob Burgdorfer</byline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean and soymeal exports in Thursday's U.S. Agriculture Department sales report fell short of estimates that circulated in U.S. oilseed markets this week but still reflected an active sales pace.</p>
<p>The sales were &quot; disappointing compared to expectations,&quot; said Charlie Sernatinger, analyst with Man International. &quot;The market was looking for close to a million tonnes of new soybean sales and a third of a million on soymeal.&quot;</p>
<p>USDA reported net soybean sales of 582,400 tonnes during the week ended October 3 and soymeal sales of 248,800 tonnes.</p>
</text>
